---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { CAC_NUMBER, CONTACT_EMAIL, CONTACT_HREF, ORG_NAME } from '../lib/site';

export const prerender = true;
---

<LegalLayout title="Terms of Service" description="The terms for using the YEA website and programmes." updated="25 October 2026">
  <p>
    These terms apply to your use of <a href="https://www.yeaimpactfoundation.top">yeaimpactfoundation.top</a> (the “website”),
    run by the {ORG_NAME} (“YEA”, “we”, “us”), registered with the Corporate Affairs Commission of Nigeria ({CAC_NUMBER}). By
    creating an account or using the website, you agree to these terms and to our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who can use YEA</h2>
  <p>
    Our programmes are for young people aged 12 to 40, and for the mentors, partners and employers who support them. If you are
    under 18, you need permission from a parent or guardian to create an account.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Your account</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Give accurate information, and keep your email address up to date.</li>
    <li>Keep your password private. You are responsible for activity on your account.</li>
    <li>One account per person.</li>
    <li>Tell us straight away at <a href={CONTACT_HREF}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> if you think someone else is using your account.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Using our programmes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Courses and events</strong> are free unless stated otherwise. Places may be limited, and we may change or cancel a course or event. If we do, we will let registered participants know.</li>
    <li><strong>Event check-in</strong> uses the QR code we give you when you register. Keep it to yourself, because it can only be used once.</li>
    <li><strong>Mentorship</strong> is offered by volunteers. Mentors decide whether to accept a request, and we cannot guarantee a match.</li>
    <li><strong>Jobs and opportunities</strong> are posted by third-party employers. We do not employ you and are not responsible for an employer’s hiring decisions. Never pay anyone to secure a job listed here, and report any request for payment to us.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>harass, threaten or exploit anyone, especially young people;</li>
    <li>post or send false, offensive or unlawful content;</li>
    <li>pretend to be someone else, or misrepresent your connection to YEA;</li>
    <li>try to access other people’s accounts or data, or disrupt the website;</li>
    <li>use the website to advertise, spam or collect other users’ information.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may suspend or close accounts that break these rules. Where someone’s safety is at risk, we may report the matter to the
    relevant authorities.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Our content</h2>
  <p>
    The YEA name, logo, course materials and other content on the website belong to YEA or our partners. You may use them for your
    own learning, but you may not copy, sell or republish them without our written permission.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Disclaimers</h2>
  <p>
    We provide the website and programmes in good faith, as they are, for educational and empowerment purposes. We work to keep
    them accurate and available, but we cannot promise they will always be error-free or uninterrupted. Our campaign content,
    including on drug abuse, is for awareness and support. It is not medical or professional advice.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    As far as the law allows, YEA is not liable for any indirect loss, or for the actions of mentors, employers or other users.
    Nothing in these terms limits any rights you have that cannot be excluded by law.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Closing your account</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us to close your account at any time by emailing <a href={CONTACT_HREF}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. We handle your data
    as described in our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms from time to time. We will change the date at the top of this page and tell account holders by
    email about any significant change. Continuing to use the website after a change means you accept the updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the Federal Republic of Nigeria.</p>

  <h2>11. Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    {ORG_NAME}<br />
    Email: <a href={CONTACT_HREF}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
